{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JVoYJt53XZvBfBAJdt1w7o","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→artifact: spec\n     3→loop: 2\n     4→project: tank-sim\n     5→backend: codex(gpt-5.4-xhigh)\n     6→role: planner\n     7→created_at: 2026-03-15T03:53:45Z\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→I’m reviewing `prompt.md`, the completed loop artifacts, and recent git checkpoints to determine what is already built and what the next unimplemented milestone should be.\n    11→The repo has no `loops/` directory in the working tree, so I’m pulling the relevant context from `spec.md`, the codebase, and the loop checkpoint commits instead.\n    12→I’ve confirmed loop 1 built the workspace, preset loading, typed state, validation, RNG, save/load, and basic snapshot plumbing. I’m reading the engine and type implementations now to separate placeholders from real milestone-2 behavior.\n    13→The current code confirms milestone-2 behavior is not implemented yet: geometry math exists, but water changes are simple retention-only mass cuts and ambient temperature still assigns the room temperature directly without a heat model. I’m checking the loop artifacts next so the planned feature stays aligned with what was already approved.\n    14→I’ve got the completed loop-1 artifacts now. The approved notes explicitly defer source-water chemistry mixing and heat-driven ambient response, which makes the next slice narrower than the original milestone name.\n    15→# Feature: Source-Water Mixing and Geometry-Driven Thermal Response\n    16→\n    17→## Description\n    18→Loop 1 already completed the workspace, deterministic state/RNG/save-load foundation, geometry helper math, snapshot derivations, preset-loading scaffolding, and the minimal queued-action engine. The next missing slice is to make those scaffolds causal: resolve scenario/source-water/process presets into runtime state, execute `WaterChangePercent` with real replacement chemistry and temperature instead of pure dilution, and update water temperature hourly from ambient air, heater settings, tank size, and lid exchange. This feature should explicitly exclude feed-to-TAN conversion, hourly DO consumption/reaeration, and broader cycling behavior for now; it exists to unlock correct water-change mass balance, ambient-temperature behavior, and the thermal half of tank-size response.\n    19→\n    20→## Acceptance Criteria\n    21→- [ ] `TankState` gains runtime-resolved setup data needed for deterministic continuation: a stable in-state source-water catalog keyed by preset `id`, resolved process parameters, and any thermal observables required by tests; these fields serialize in save files and schema version is bumped if compatibility is broken.\n    22→- [ ] `tank_scenarios::seeded_state` or a builder it delegates to materializes scenario presets into non-default state: scenario geometry populates `TankGeometry`, `environment.ambient_temp_c` comes from the scenario, initial `WaterState` totals come from the selected source-water profile multiplied by current fill volume, and substrate/plant state is derived from preset IDs instead of leaving `TankState::new` defaults in place.\n    23→- [ ] Source-water presets stop using GH/KH/TDS summary values as hidden source-of-truth. Each preset carries explicit per-liter values for TAN, nitrite, nitrate, phosphate, DIC, DOC, DON, alkalinity, Ca, Mg, Na, K, HCO3, Cl, SO4, and temperature; loader validation rejects non-finite or negative chemistry and documents any derived-value tolerance.\n    24→- [ ] `WaterChangePercent` removes exactly `percent / 100.0` of each tracked dissolved total, then adds replacement mass from the referenced source-water profile using exchanged liters. `0%` water changes are no-ops.\n    25→- [ ] Water changes also mix water temperature by exchanged volume. Replacing `50%` of the tank with colder or warmer source water shifts `water.temperature_c` proportionally and does not jump to source temperature unless `percent = 100`.\n    26→- [ ] Partial-failure invariant: if a queued water change references an unknown source profile or invalid resolved profile, `step_hours` returns a typed `SimError` and leaves `TankState`, queued actions, RNG state, `day`, `hour_of_day`, and `event_log` exactly unchanged. No partial mass removal, temperature mixing, or event emission is allowed.\n    27→- [ ] The hourly temperature step uses the prompt’s discrete heat model with `dt_s = 3600.0`, `heat_capacity_j_per_k = volume_l * 4186.0`, `ua_total_w_per_k = (k_surface * surface_area_m2 * top_factor) + (k_wall * wall_area_m2)`, `q_ambient_w = ua_total_w_per_k * (ambient_temp_c - water_temp_c)`, heater output only when enabled and below `setpoint_c - deadband_c / 2.0`, and `delta_temp_c = (q_ambient_w + q_heater_w) * dt_s / heat_capacity_j_per_k`.\n    28→- [ ] Existing geometry helpers drive the heat model. Smaller tanks respond faster than larger tanks, and `open_top = false` applies the existing lid multiplier to slow surface heat exchange relative to an open-top tank under the same conditions.\n    29→- [ ] `ChangeAmbientTemperature` changes only `environment.ambient_temp_c`; water temperature changes gradually on later ticks. If ambient exceeds heater setpoint, heater output eventually becomes `0.0` and never goes negative.\n    30→- [ ] A reusable `do_sat_mg_l` helper or observable is added using linear interpolation over `0 C -> 14.6`, `10 C -> 11.3`, `20 C -> 9.1`, `30 C -> 7.6`. Full DO mass updates remain out of scope for this feature, but the saturation target must be inspectable by tests and later systems.\n    31→- [ ] `ro_like` acts as the zero-nutrient reference water for regression tests: a `50%` water change using it reduces `ammonia_total_mg_n_total`, `nitrite_mg_n_total`, `nitrate_mg_n_total`, `phosphate_mg_p_total`, `dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total`, and total tracked ions by `50% +/- 0.5%`.\n    32→- [ ] Regression coverage is added for deterministic scenario materialization, `water_change_mass_balance`, `ambient_temperature_action`, and the thermal half of tank-size response (`10 L` reaches half of its eventual ambient-step delta in fewer than half as many ticks as `100 L`). The feed-pulse TAN half of `tank_size_response` remains blocked by later nitrogen-cycle work.\n    33→\n    34→## Files to Modify/Create\n    35→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/source_water.rs` - runtime source-water profile with per-liter chemistry and conversion helpers\n    36→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` - runtime process parameters for heat-transfer coefficients and later chemistry systems\n    37→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/mod.rs` - export new runtime setup types\n    38→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` - persist resolved source-water catalog, process params, and thermal observables in `TankState`\n    39→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs` - add initial-fill and water-change mixing helpers\n    40→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/hardware.rs` - expose last heater output or equivalent heater-runtime field\n    41→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` - surface thermal observables needed by tests and the future TUI\n    42→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/actions.rs` - add typed lookup/resolution errors for water-change failures\n    43→- `crates/tank_core/src/save.rs` - bump schema/version handling if expanded runtime state changes save compatibility\n    44→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/temperature.rs` - geometry-driven heat transfer and DO saturation target helper\n    45→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/water_change.rs` - exact source-water mixing logic and atomic application rules\n    46→- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` - wire water-change and temperature systems into the hourly tick order\n    47→- `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` - expand `SourceWaterPreset` and `ProcessParamsPreset` schemas and validation\n    48→- `crates/tank_data/data/source_water/*.toml` - explicit source-water chemistry, with `ro_like` as the zero-nutrient reference\n    49→- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` - add heat-transfer coefficients used by the hourly model\n    50→- `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` - build resolved `TankState` from scenario, source-water, substrate, plant, and process presets\n    51→- `crates/tank_core/tests/water_change_mass_balance.rs` - exact water-change regression\n    52→- `crates/tank_core/tests/ambient_temperature_action.rs` - gradual-warming and heater-cutoff regression\n    53→- `crates/tank_core/tests/tank_size_thermal_response.rs` - geometry-dependent thermal response regression\n    54→- `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` - extend roundtrip coverage to include new runtime setup and thermal fields\n    55→- `crates/tank_scenarios/tests/materialization.rs` - scenario-to-state resolution regression\n    56→\n    57→## Dependencies\n    58→- Requires: Workspace Skeleton, Core Types, RNG, and Save/Load\n    59→- Blocks: Nitrogen Cycle and Dissolved Oxygen Dynamics; full `tank_size_response`; scenario-backed manual play and later biology systems\n    60→\n    61→---\n    62→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"c8288857-81aa-496b-b72f-2ac78bfa4841"}
