{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01145cKxbFiksu3TUajX1MeU","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→artifact: spec\n     3→loop: 3\n     4→project: tank-sim\n     5→backend: claude(opus)\n     6→role: planner\n     7→created_at: 2026-03-15T04:28:43Z\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→Now I have a complete picture. Let me write the spec for Loop 3, which corresponds to Milestone 3.\n    11→\n    12→# Feature: Dissolved Pool Dynamics, DO Model, pH Updates, and Event Emission\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→Implement the hourly dissolved-pool update systems that make water chemistry dynamic. This loop adds: (1) light-state computation, (2) reaeration driving dissolved oxygen toward saturation, (3) background biological oxygen demand from existing biomass, (4) hourly pH/alkalinity/DIC updates so pH is no longer static, (5) NH3 speciation as a runtime utility usable during simulation (not just at snapshot time), and (6) threshold-based event emission for `AmmoniaWarning`, `NitriteWarning`, and `OxygenDip`. These systems form the foundation that Milestone 4 (decomposition, nitrification, cycling) will build upon. No nitrogen-cycle transformation (TAN→NO2→NO3) or detritus decomposition is included here — those belong to Loop 4.\n    16→\n    17→## Acceptance Criteria\n    18→- [ ] A helper `is_light_on(hour_of_day: u8, photoperiod_hours: f64) -> bool` exists and is used in the hourly pipeline; light is centered on noon (hour 12), so an 8-hour photoperiod means hours 8–15 are lit\n    19→- [ ] Reaeration system updates `dissolved_oxygen_mg_total` each tick: `delta_do = kLa * (do_sat - do_mg_l) * volume_l * dt_h` where `dt_h = 1.0`, `kLa` scales with `top_exchange_factor` and aeration intensity\n    20→- [ ] Background biological oxygen demand (BOD) is subtracted hourly: a small per-hour respiration draw proportional to total biomass (shrimp count, plant biomass, microbe biomass, algae biomass) so that DO can drop at night when photosynthesis is off\n    21→- [ ] During lit hours, a small net photosynthetic O2 contribution is added from existing plant + periphyton biomass (simple proportional rate, not full plant-growth model — that is Loop 5)\n    22→- [ ] DO is clamped to non-negative by the existing invariant system (no negative oxygen)\n    23→- [ ] DIC and alkalinity are nudged hourly by a small background respiration/photosynthesis delta so pH drifts realistically (respiration adds DIC; photosynthesis during lit hours removes DIC)\n    24→- [ ] pH is recomputed from alkalinity and DIC each tick using the existing `6.3 + log10(alk) - log10(dic)` formula, stored as `state.water.ph` (new field), so downstream systems can read it without recomputing\n    25→- [ ] NH3 speciation helper `compute_nh3_mg_l(tan_mg_l, ph, temp_c) -> f64` exists in a shared location and is used by both the event emitter and `TankSnapshot`\n    26→- [ ] After each hourly tick, event emission checks run:\n    27→  - `AmmoniaWarning` if `nh3_mg_l >= 0.02` (with cause `HighAmmonia`)\n    28→  - `NitriteWarning` if `nitrite_mg_l >= 0.5` (with cause `HighNitrite`)\n    29→  - `OxygenDip` if `do_mg_l < 4.0` (with cause `LowOxygen`)\n    30→  - Events are emitted at most once per day per kind to avoid log spam (track last-emitted day per kind)\n    31→- [ ] `ProcessParams` is extended with new fields: `reaeration_kla_base`, `aeration_kla_boost`, `background_bod_mg_o2_per_g_biomass_per_hour`, `plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour`, `respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`, `photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour`\n    32→- [ ] Night oxygen dips are observable: a tank with plants and shrimp, run for 48 hours, shows lower DO at night hours than during the photoperiod\n    33→- [ ] Aeration effect is observable: with aeration enabled at high intensity, DO recovers faster toward saturation than without\n    34→- [ ] `save_load_resume` test still passes (new state fields serialize/deserialize correctly)\n    35→- [ ] `determinism_same_seed` still holds (new systems are deterministic, no thread-local RNG)\n    36→- [ ] All existing tests continue to pass\n    37→\n    38→## Files to Modify/Create\n    39→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs` — new file: `is_light_on` helper\n    40→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs` — new file: reaeration, BOD, photosynthetic O2\n    41→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` — new file: hourly pH/DIC/alkalinity update, `compute_nh3_mg_l` helper\n    42→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs` — new file: threshold-based event emission with daily dedup\n    43→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/mod.rs` — add `pub mod light; pub mod dissolved_oxygen; pub mod chemistry; pub mod events;`\n    44→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` — extend `ProcessParams` with reaeration, BOD, and DIC rate fields\n    45→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` — add `last_event_day: BTreeMap<String, u32>` (or similar) for daily dedup tracking\n    46→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/water.rs` — add `pub ph: f64` field to `WaterState`, initialize from DIC/alkalinity\n    47→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` — read `state.water.ph` instead of recomputing; use shared `compute_nh3_mg_l`\n    48→- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — wire new systems into `step_one_hour` at the correct pipeline positions (steps 5, 9, 10, 11-partial, 13)\n    49→- `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs` — add pH range clamp (5.5..=8.5) to invariant checks\n    50→- `crates/tank_core/tests/dissolved_oxygen.rs` — new test file: night dip test, aeration boost test, reaeration convergence\n    51→- `crates/tank_core/tests/chemistry.rs` — new test file: pH drift test, NH3 speciation correctness\n    52→- `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` — new test file: threshold emission, daily dedup, cause_codes non-empty\n    53→\n    54→## Dependencies\n    55→- Requires: Loop 2 (geometry, temperature, water changes, DO saturation lookup)\n    56→- Blocks: Loop 4 (decomposition + nitrification will consume O2, produce/consume alkalinity, and generate TAN that triggers AmmoniaWarning events)\n    57→\n    58→---\n    59→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"ae886c10-7975-4ec4-806a-c7a8fe09789d"}
