{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GpQtzxkH3H3GFAFBf27X1J","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→---\n     2→artifact: spec\n     3→loop: 4\n     4→project: tank-sim\n     5→backend: codex(gpt-5.4-xhigh)\n     6→role: planner\n     7→created_at: 2026-03-15T04:47:09Z\n     8→---\n     9→\n    10→I’m checking the current prompt, completed loop specs, and recent git checkpoints to map what is already delivered before selecting the next feature.\n    11→I’ve confirmed the branch is at the checkpoint after loop 3 planning. Next I’m narrowing to the actual source tree and prior loop specs so I can avoid proposing something already built.\n    12→The workspace doesn’t contain a `loops/` directory in the checkout, so I’m using the branch history and current source/tests as the authoritative record of completed work. Now I’m reading the core manifests and engine modules to verify what loop 3 actually delivered.\n    13→I found the actual loop artifacts under `.ralph/projects/tank-sim/loops`, so I’m switching to those instead of the missing top-level `loops/` path. I’m reading the prompt and the approved loop specs now to line up the next feature with the mandated milestone sequence.\n    14→I have the approved scope for loops 1 through 3. I’m now verifying the current engine and biology state directly so the next spec only covers genuinely missing milestone-4 behavior, not placeholder fields that already exist.\n    15→The current engine confirms loops 1–3 stop at feed queuing, thermal/chemistry updates, and threshold events. There is still no decomposition, nitrification, daily biology, or cycling behavior in the hourly pipeline, so I’m checking the tests next to define the next feature around the first missing acceptance coverage rather than broader future work.\n    16→I’m at the point of drafting the next loop. Before I lock it in, I’m checking the event/action enums and process/source-water schemas so the spec names the exact extension points already present in the code instead of inventing parallel structures.\n    17→I’ve confirmed the next missing slice is Milestone 4. I’m doing one last check of the loop-4 temp planner log and git status just to ensure there isn’t already an approved or partially committed spec for the same feature that I should avoid duplicating.\n    18→# Feature: Detritus Mineralization, Nitrifier Guild Cycling, and Biofilter Maturation\n    19→\n    20→## Description\n    21→Approved loop artifacts and git history show loops 1-3 are complete: loop 1 established the workspace, deterministic state/RNG, preset loading, and save/load; loop 2 added source-water mixing plus geometry-driven thermal response; loop 3 added hourly light state, DO dynamics, pH/DIC drift, NH3 speciation, and warning events. The next missing mandatory slice is the live nitrogen cycle. Current code has detritus and microbial state placeholders, but feed still only accumulates waste and no system converts that waste into dissolved organics, TAN, nitrite, or nitrate. This feature should implement Milestone 4 only: decomposer-driven mineralization, AOB/NOB/comammox kinetics, oxygen and alkalinity coupling, seeded-vs-unseeded cycling behavior, and the feed-pulse TAN concentration response. It should explicitly defer loop-5 plant/algae growth and loop-6 shrimp reproduction/mortality work.\n    22→\n    23→## Acceptance Criteria\n    24→- [ ] `Engine::step_one_hour` gains a dedicated nitrogen-cycle phase between light-state resolution and the existing chemistry/DO/event phases; within that phase the order is feed leaching, detritus breakdown/mineralization, then nitrification and guild growth/decay.\n    25→- [ ] Feed no longer creates instant dissolved nitrogen; `PlayerAction::Feed` may still add particulate mass immediately, but TAN, nitrite, and nitrate must change only through the subsequent pathway `particulate_organics_g_total -> fine_detritus_g_total -> dissolved_feed_residue_g_total` or an equivalent short-lived leach pool -> `dissolved_organic_* -> ammonia_total_mg_n_total -> nitrite_mg_n_total -> nitrate_mg_n_total`.\n    26→- [ ] Decomposition/mineralization rates are driven by `microbe.decomposer_biomass_g`, bounded environmental factors such as temperature and dissolved oxygen, and new process coefficients; rate clamps must prevent consuming more particulate, fine detritus, DOC, or DON than exists.\n    27→- [ ] `SiphonDetritus { fraction }` continues to affect only detritus pools, but it now has visible downstream cycling consequences by reducing later mineralization pressure; it must not directly remove dissolved TAN, nitrite, or nitrate.\n    28→- [ ] `ProcessParams` and the default process TOML gain the kinetic inputs needed for detritus breakdown and nitrification, including half-saturation constants, guild-specific `vmax`, growth/decay yields, a lower comammox multiplier, and any feed stoichiometry constants; preset validation rejects non-finite or negative values.\n    29→- [ ] Nitrification is split into ammonia oxidizers, nitrite oxidizers, and comammox using bounded Monod-style rates `rate = vmax * biomass * maturity_factor * f_temp * f_pH * f_do * substrate / (k_substrate + substrate)`; realized rates must be biomass-limited, oxygen-limited, slower in immature or dirty filters, and comammox must use a lower `vmax` than the TAN->nitrite path.\n    30→- [ ] Realized nitrification consumes dissolved oxygen at `4.57 mg O2` per `1 mg N` oxidized to nitrate and alkalinity at `0.1428 meq` per `1 mg N`; if TAN, nitrite, DO, or alkalinity is insufficient, only the supported fraction may convert and all coupled pools must remain finite and non-negative after the tick.\n    31→- [ ] A chemistry regression proves active nitrification lowers alkalinity and pH relative to an otherwise identical non-nitrifying control, while invariant enforcement keeps pH within `5.5..=8.5`.\n    32→- [ ] Microbial guild biomass changes over time: realized mineralization/oxidation drives growth, starvation or low-oxygen conditions drive decay, and `CleanFilter { intensity }` produces a proportional setback in active decomposer and nitrifier biomass so post-cleaning TAN/nitrite control worsens temporarily.\n    33→- [ ] A daily update hook runs every 24 hourly ticks to recompute `filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index` from current guild biomass/capacity, clamp it to `0.0..=1.0`, and emit `BiofilmMaturityIncrease` or `CycleProgressing` with non-empty `cause_codes` when maturity meaningfully improves; the existing per-day warning dedup behavior must remain intact.\n    34→- [ ] Failure-mode invariant: if any cycle sub-rate becomes non-finite or a limiter collapses to zero, that sub-rate is treated as `0.0` for the tick, unaffected substeps continue deterministically, and the tick still ends with finite non-negative dissolved pools, detritus pools, and microbial biomasses.\n    35→- [ ] `tank_scenarios` exposes a deterministic seeded/unseeded cycling fixture pair or builder so regressions can create two otherwise identical tanks that differ only in starting biofilter seeding inputs.\n    36→- [ ] `cycling_seeded_vs_unseeded` regression is added: the seeded tank reaches `tan_mg_l < 0.1` and `nitrite_mg_l < 0.1` earlier than the unseeded tank, and the unseeded tank shows non-zero TAN and nitrite peaks.\n    37→- [ ] The feed-pulse half of `tank_size_response` is added or completed: after the same feed pulse, peak `tan_mg_l` in a `10 L` tank is at least `5x` the peak in an otherwise identical `100 L` tank.\n    38→- [ ] `event_generation` regression is added or completed using a warm, overfed, weak-aeration setup; it must emit at least one of `AmmoniaWarning` or `OxygenDip` with non-empty `cause_codes`, without depending on loop-5 algae logic.\n    39→- [ ] Save/load and determinism regressions continue to pass with active cycle state, and all loop-1 through loop-3 tests remain green.\n    40→\n    41→## Files to Modify/Create\n    42→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/nitrogen_cycle.rs` - new hourly detritus leaching, mineralization, nitrification, and microbial growth/decay system\n    43→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/mod.rs` - export the new nitrogen-cycle module\n    44→- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` - insert the cycle phase into the hourly pipeline and add the first daily biofilter-maturity update hook\n    45→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs` - apply nitrification oxygen demand without double-counting background respiration\n    46→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs` - apply nitrification alkalinity demand before pH recomputation and add any shared cycle chemistry helpers\n    47→- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/events.rs` - add cycle-progress and biofilm-maturity event emission rules\n    48→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` - extend runtime process parameters with detritus and nitrifier kinetics\n    49→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs` - wire `MicrobeState` and `DetritusState` into active cycling, including any short-lived residue pool changes\n    50→- `crates/tank_core/src/types/state.rs` - persist any daily cycle-summary or threshold-tracking state needed for maturity updates/events\n    51→- `crates/tank_core/src/invariants.rs` - enforce non-negative and finite guarantees for active cycle fields\n    52→- `crates/tank_data/src/presets.rs` - extend process preset schema and validation for cycle kinetics\n    53→- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` - provide default mineralization and nitrifier parameters\n    54→- `crates/tank_scenarios/src/lib.rs` - add deterministic seeded and unseeded cycling fixtures/builders\n    55→- `crates/tank_core/tests/cycling.rs` - new cycling regressions for seeded vs unseeded behavior, filter-cleaning setback, and limiter correctness\n    56→- `crates/tank_core/tests/chemistry.rs` - add nitrification alkalinity/pH regression coverage\n    57→- `crates/tank_core/tests/tank_size_thermal_response.rs` - add the feed-pulse TAN concentration regression\n    58→- `crates/tank_core/tests/events.rs` - extend event coverage for cycle-progress and warm overfeeding warning generation\n    59→- `crates/tank_core/tests/save_load.rs` - verify save/load determinism with active cycle state\n    60→- `crates/tank_scenarios/tests/materialization.rs` - verify cycling fixtures are deterministic and differ only in seeding inputs\n    61→\n    62→## Dependencies\n    63→- Requires: Dissolved Pool Dynamics, DO Model, pH Updates, and Event Emission\n    64→- Blocks: Substrate, plants, and algae/periphyton dynamics; shrimp population/reproduction; TUI MVP and remaining v1 acceptance work\n    65→\n    66→---\n    67→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"fcbf2714-d879-4793-9ee1-1e86d12f3c4d"}
