{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EHMQAkq2y56AbN7BJpGyvd","type":"tool_result","content":"5:Target system: freshwater planted shrimp tank (`Neocaridina davidi`)  \n13:Build a Rust simulation engine that models a living freshwater planted aquarium as an ecosystem rather than a scripted set of events.\n20:- observe chemistry, plant growth, algae, biofilm, microfauna, shrimp condition, and long-term stabilization\n24:  - algae blooms\n47:- rooted plants\n49:- free algae\n70:- additional plant archetypes\n87:- plant vs algae competition\n99:- Rising temperature interacts with nutrient availability and can shift the plant/algae balance.\n140:- at least two plant guilds\n141:- at least two algae/biofilm guilds\n222:  - footprint and substrate depth affect rooted plant biomass capacity\n271:- plant growth\n272:- algae growth\n312:    pub plants: Vec<PlantGuildState>,\n313:    pub algae: AlgaeState,\n343:- plant/algae rates\n461:- nutrient-rich planted substrate\n510:- one rooted/substrate-responsive plant guild\n516:    pub suspended_algae_biomass: f32,   // green water\n517:    pub surface_film_biomass: f32,      // glass/film algae\n518:    pub periphyton_biomass: f32,        // attached biofilm + algae complex\n600:- plant health and growth direction\n601:- algae risk\n661:- plant uptake\n669:- plant uptake\n723:- plant photosynthesis (light-dependent)\n730:- plant respiration\n746:- night-time oxygen can dip in planted tanks\n769:- do not hardcode pH as constant if plants, nitrification, and water changes occur\n794:- algae/periphyton competition\n800:plant_growth = biomass\n810:- fast stem plants: stronger water-column nutrient uptake, faster growth, stronger shading feedback\n811:- root-feeding plants: benefit more from nutrient-rich sediment and adequate substrate depth\n813:- floating plants: strong light access, strong nutrient uptake, high shading effect\n816:Nutrient-rich substrate must benefit rooted plants more than inert substrate.\n821:- suspended algae\n829:- weak plant competition\n835:algae_growth = biomass\n852:Periphyton is not merely “algae.” It is a mixed guild that includes autotrophs and heterotrophs and should be treated as an ecological intermediary.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"f1311ee8-63a0-4344-97f1-2bb09930df32"}
