{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EmDxQcrT2PXbGPSWJW4tM8","type":"tool_result","content":"   784→## 10.7 Plant growth\n   785→\n   786→Plants should not just be decorative biomass.\n   787→\n   788→Plant growth must depend on:\n   789→- available light\n   790→- water temperature\n   791→- nutrient availability\n   792→- access to nutrients from water and/or substrate depending on guild\n   793→- self-shading\n   794→- algae/periphyton competition\n   795→- stress from poor chemistry\n   796→\n   797→Recommended rate structure:\n   798→\n   799→```text\n   800→plant_growth = biomass\n   801→             * f_light\n   802→             * f_temp\n   803→             * min(f_nitrogen, f_phosphorus, f_carbon)\n   804→             * habitat_factor\n   805→             - respiration\n   806→             - senescence\n   807→```\n   808→\n   809→### Guild differences\n   810→- fast stem plants: stronger water-column nutrient uptake, faster growth, stronger shading feedback\n   811→- root-feeding plants: benefit more from nutrient-rich sediment and adequate substrate depth\n   812→- moss/epiphytes: more surface-attached, low root dependence\n   813→- floating plants: strong light access, strong nutrient uptake, high shading effect\n   814→\n   815→### Required behavior\n   816→Nutrient-rich substrate must benefit rooted plants more than inert substrate.\n   817→\n   818→## 10.8 Algae and periphyton\n   819→\n   820→Separate at least:\n   821→- suspended algae\n   822→- attached film/periphyton\n   823→\n   824→Growth drivers:\n   825→- light\n   826→- excess nutrients\n   827→- temperature\n   828→- low grazing pressure\n   829→- weak plant competition\n   830→- surface availability (for attached forms)\n   831→\n   832→Recommended structure:\n   833→\n   834→```text\n   835→algae_growth = biomass\n   836→             * f_light\n   837→             * f_temp\n   838→             * min(f_nitrogen, f_phosphorus)\n   839→             * competition_modifier\n   840→             - grazing\n   841→             - sloughing\n   842→```\n   843→\n   844→### Required behavior\n   845→The system must support:\n   846→- green-water style blooms when nutrients/light are favorable\n   847→- film/periphyton increase on surfaces under imbalance\n   848→- attached biofilm as both nuisance and shrimp food source\n   849→\n   850→## 10.9 Biofilm / periphyton role\n   851→\n   852→Periphyton is not merely “algae.” It is a mixed guild that includes autotrophs and heterotrophs and should be treated as an ecological intermediary.\n   853→\n   854→Periphyton must:\n   855→- provide shrimp grazing resource\n   856→- contribute to oxygen and nutrient dynamics\n   857→- increase with available surface area and light/nutrients\n   858→- support microfauna habitat\n   859→- become nuisance at high biomass\n   860→\n   861→## 10.10 Decomposition and mineralization\n   862→\n   863→Detritus must move through at least these pools:\n   864→\n   865→```text\n   866→particulate food/waste -> fine detritus -> dissolved organics -> mineralized nutrients\n   867→```\n   868→\n   869→Rates depend on:\n   870→- temperature\n   871→- decomposer biomass\n   872→- oxygen\n   873→- detritus quality\n   874→- substrate trapping\n   875→\n   876→Overfeeding must increase:\n   877→- detritus\n   878→- microbial oxygen demand\n   879→- TAN generation\n   880→- algae risk\n   881→\n   882→## 10.11 Microfauna\n   883→\n   884→Microfauna should be abstracted as guilds with real effects.\n   885→\n   886→Minimum effects:\n   887→- bacterivorous protists reduce bacterial standing biomass but enhance nutrient turnover\n   888→- rotifers/nematodes/microcrustaceans compete for biofilm resources\n   889→- shrimp grazing/predation suppresses some microfauna pools\n   890→\n   891→Player does not need exact counts, but the engine must use these pools in ecology.\n   892→\n   893→## 10.12 Shrimp physiology and population\n   894→\n   895→`Neocaridina davidi` is the target reference species for v1.\n   896→\n   897→The shrimp model must include:\n   898→- adults\n   899→- juveniles\n   900→- berried females\n   901→- condition\n   902→- molt stress\n   903→- reproduction readiness\n   904→- juvenile survival\n   905→\n   906→### Inputs affecting shrimp condition\n   907→- food availability\n   908→- biofilm availability\n   909→- temperature\n   910→- DO\n   911→- NH3 risk\n   912→- nitrite risk\n   913→- mineral status (GH / ion adequacy proxy)\n   914→- instability / sudden swings\n   915→\n   916→### Reproduction\n   917→A simple but meaningful model:\n   918→\n   919→```text\n   920→spawn_probability =\n   921→    f_temperature\n   922→  * f_condition\n   923→  * f_stability\n   924→  * f_mineral_status\n   925→  * sex_ratio_proxy\n   926→```\n   927→\n   928→When spawning succeeds:\n   929→- berried female count increases\n   930→- egg development progresses over days\n   931→- hatch success depends on stress during egg period\n   932→\n   933→### Molting\n   934→Molting stress rises when:\n   935→- mineral conditions are poor\n   936→- temperature is stressful\n   937→- rapid chemistry swings occur\n   938→- condition is poor\n   939→\n   940→### Mortality\n   941→Mortality should be probabilistic, with risk increased by:\n   942→- NH3\n   943→- severe nitrite\n   944→- low oxygen\n   945→- prolonged thermal stress\n   946→- failed molt stress\n   947→- starvation / collapse of biofilm and food web\n   948→\n   949→---\n   950→\n   951→## 11. Player actions\n   952→\n   953→Actions are part of the simulation API.\n   954→\n   955→## 11.1 Setup actions\n   956→\n   957→- choose tank dimensions and fill height\n   958→- choose substrate type(s) and depth\n   959→- choose filter and media\n   960→- choose heater and setpoint\n   961→- choose light intensity and photoperiod\n   962→- define source water chemistry\n   963→- add plants\n   964→- add shrimp\n   965→- optionally seed filter/media\n   966→\n   967→## 11.2 Runtime husbandry actions\n   968→\n   969→The engine MUST support at least:\n   970→\n   971→```rust\n   972→pub enum PlayerAction {\n   973→    Feed { grams: f32 },\n   974→    WaterChangePercent { percent: f32, source: SourceWaterProfile },\n   975→    TopOffEvaporation { liters: f32, source: SourceWaterProfile },\n   976→    DoseFertilizer { n_mg: f32, p_mg: f32, k_mg: f32 },\n   977→    TrimPlants { fraction: f32 },\n   978→    SiphonDetritus { fraction: f32 },\n   979→    CleanFilter { intensity: f32 },\n   980→    AddShrimp { count: u32 },\n   981→    RemoveShrimp { count: u32 },\n   982→    ChangePhotoperiod { hours: f32 },\n   983→    ChangeLightIntensity { intensity_index: f32 },"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"04c45f7c-741b-47ab-bb5c-c69f1f935b65"}
