{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013aSVJ6RroqQ847pQy5QRmW","type":"tool_result","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed report.\n\n## Summary: Tank Simulation Project - Current State Analysis\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the tank simulation project to understand what has been implemented for Milestone 5 (substrate, plants, algae/periphyton). Here's what I found:\n\n### Current Loop Status\nThe project has **successfully completed Loops 1-4**:\n- **Loop 1**: Workspace skeleton, core types, RNG, save/load ✓\n- **Loop 2**: Source water mixing and thermal response ✓\n- **Loop 3**: Dissolved pool dynamics, DO model, pH updates, event emission ✓\n- **Loop 4**: Detritus mineralization, nitrifier guild cycling, biofilter maturation ✓\n\nThe next milestone to implement is **Loop 5 / Milestone 5: Substrate, Plants, Algae/Periphyton**.\n\n---\n\n### What EXISTS (Already Implemented)\n\n#### 1. **Substrate Types & State Structure**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs`\n\n```rust\npub enum SubstrateKind {\n    InertSand,\n    InertGravel,\n    ActivePlanted,\n    CoarsePorous,\n}\n\npub struct SubstrateLayerState {\n    pub kind: SubstrateKind,\n    pub depth_cm: f64,\n    pub nutrient_store_mg_n_total: f64,\n    pub nutrient_store_mg_p_total: f64,\n    pub cation_exchange_capacity_index: f64,\n    pub detritus_trapping_index: f64,\n    pub colonizable_area_cm2: f64,\n    pub low_oxygen_tendency_index: f64,\n    pub grazing_surface_index: f64,\n}\n```\n\n**Key point**: The structure is fully defined with physical properties but **nutrient stores are NOT USED in any update system yet**. They're placeholders.\n\n#### 2. **Plant Guild Types & State**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`\n\n```rust\npub enum PlantGuild {\n    FastStem,\n    RootFeedingRosette,\n}\n\npub struct PlantGuildState {\n    pub guild: PlantGuild,\n    pub biomass_g: f64,\n    pub health_index: f64,\n    pub crowding_index: f64,\n    pub habitat_index: f64,\n}\n```\n\n**Status**: \n- Defined but **no growth/decay system exists**\n- `TankState` always initializes with 2 default plant guilds (8g total at default seed)\n- Biomass changes only via `PlayerAction::TrimPlants { fraction }` action\n- **No nutrient uptake, light dependence, or growth mechanics**\n\n#### 3. **Algae & Periphyton Types**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct AlgaeState {\n    pub suspended_biomass_g: f64,          // green water\n    pub periphyton_biomass_g: f64,          // attached biofilm + algae complex\n    pub nuisance_index: f64,                // trouble indicator\n}\n```\n\n**Status**:\n- Defined but **completely inert** in the hourly update pipeline\n- Default: 0g suspended, 0.2g periphyton, 0.1 nuisance_index\n- **No growth, decay, light response, or nutrient interaction**\n\n#### 4. **Periphyton Used in O2/DIC Calculations**\n**Files**: \n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs`\n\n```rust\npub(crate) fn photosynthetic_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    plant_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g  // <-- both contribute\n}\n\npub(crate) fn respiring_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    let algae_biomass_g = state.algae.suspended_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g;\n    let microbe_biomass_g = /* ... */;\n    let shrimp_biomass_g = /* ... */;\n    // All contribute to O2 demand and DIC respiration\n}\n```\n\n**Status**: Plants and algae **do respire and photosynthesize** (affecting DO and DIC/pH hourly), but they **don't grow or change biomass**.\n\n#### 5. **Plant/Algae Snapshot Exposure**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct TankSnapshot {\n    // ... water chemistry fields ...\n    pub total_plant_biomass_g: f64,  // aggregated plant guild biomass\n    // ... no algae exposure in snapshot yet\n}\n```\n\n#### 6. **Process Parameters for Plants/Algae**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct ProcessParams {\n    pub plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour: f64,  // rate per g plant biomass\n    pub respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour: f64,\n    pub photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour: f64,\n    // ... no plant-growth kinetics yet\n}\n```\n\nDefault values: `plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour = 0.2`.\n\n#### 7. **TOML Presets Exist**\n**Substrate presets** (`/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/`):\n- `inert_sand.toml`: cEC=0.1, detritus_trap=0.3, no nutrient charge\n- `inert_gravel.toml`: similar\n- `active_planted.toml`: cEC=0.9, detritus_trap=0.6, N=60mg, P=18mg charge\n- `coarse_porous.toml`: similar structure\n\n**Plant presets** (`/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/plants/`):\n- `fast_stem.toml`: growth_rate_index=0.9, water_column_uptake=0.9, substrate_uptake=0.2\n- `root_rosette.toml`: growth_rate_index=0.6, water_column_uptake=0.3, substrate_uptake=0.9\n\n**Status**: Presets are **loaded and structured** but **not used during simulation** — they're only metadata.\n\n#### 8. **Player Actions**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`\n\nThe `TrimPlants { fraction }` action is **partially implemented**:\n```rust\nPlayerAction::TrimPlants { fraction } => {\n    for plant in &mut self.state.plant_guilds {\n        plant.biomass_g *= 1.0 - fraction;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis simply **scales biomass down** without regrowth mechanics.\n\n#### 9. **Light System**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs`\n\n```rust\npub fn is_light_on(hour_of_day: u8, photoperiod_hours: f64) -> bool {\n    let start = (12.0 - photoperiod_hours / 2.0) as u8;\n    let end = (12.0 + photoperiod_hours / 2.0) as u8;\n    hour_of_day >= start && hour_of_day < end\n}\n```\n\nLight state is **computed hourly** and passed through the DO and DIC systems, but **plants don't have light-dependent growth**.\n\n---\n\n### What DOES NOT EXIST (Needs Implementation for Milestone 5)\n\n#### 1. **Plant Growth System**\n- **No hourly/daily plant biomass update** based on:\n  - Available light (f_light)\n  - Water temperature (f_temp)\n  - Nutrient availability from water column vs substrate (guild-dependent)\n  - Self-shading and competition\n  - Health/stress modifiers\n- **No respiration-driven senescence**\n- **No habitat-index driving growth potential**\n- **Guild differences are NOT used** (fast-stem should grow faster under water-column nutrients, root-feeder should benefit more from substrate)\n\n#### 2. **Substrate Nutrient Dynamics**\n- Substrate `nutrient_store_mg_n_total` and `nutrient_store_mg_p_total` are **defined but never change**\n- **No plant nutrient uptake from substrate**\n- **No cation-exchange capacity used** (cEC index exists but inactive)\n- **No detritus trapping** (detritus_trapping_index exists but unused)\n- **No microbial activity in substrate microzones**\n\n#### 3. **Algae Growth System**\n- `AlgaeState` (suspended and periphyton) **never changes**\n- **No growth rate formula** based on:\n  - Excess nutrients (N, P) relative to plant uptake\n  - Light availability\n  - Temperature\n  - Grazing pressure (no microfauna system yet)\n  - Competition with plants\n- **No algae bloom mechanic** when plants are weak and nutrients available\n- **No periphyton buildup on surfaces** with increasing colonizable area\n\n#### 4. **Competition Mechanics**\n- **No plant vs algae trade-off** based on light, nutrients, crowding\n- `crowding_index` and `habitat_index` on plants **exist but unused**\n- `nuisance_index` on algae **exists but unused**\n\n#### 5. **Nutrient Uptake Pathways**\n- Water-column nutrients (N, P) are **never removed by plants**\n- Substrate nutrients are **never consumed by plants**\n- **No guild-specific uptake bias** (water-column vs substrate preference)\n- Plants can't compete for scarce nutrients (all growth is zero anyway)\n\n#### 6. **Update Pipeline Integration**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`\n\nThe hourly `step_one_hour` pipeline includes:\n1. Water temperature update\n2. Light state computation\n3. Nitrogen cycle (feed → detritus → mineralization → nitrification)\n4. Chemistry (DIC, alkalinity, pH)\n5. Dissolved oxygen (reaeration, BOD, photosynthetic O2)\n6. Event emission\n\n**Missing**: \n- **No plant growth step** after nutrient/light availability is known\n- **No algae growth step** competing with plants\n- **No daily substrate biogeochemistry** (microbial activity, nutrient cycling)\n- **No plant senescence or stress response to poor conditions**\n\n#### 7. **Linked Systems Not Yet Integrated**\nEven though substrate layer properties are defined, they're not used because:\n- **Periphyton colonizable area** (`colonizable_area_cm2`) is static in SubstrateLayerState\n- **Grazing surface index** doesn't drive microfauna-plant-algae food web (microfauna system is Loop 6)\n- **Low oxygen tendency** in substrate exists but no anoxic microzones are modeled\n- **Detritus trapping** doesn't feed back into local mineralization rates\n\n#### 8. **Acceptance Tests**\nNo tests exist for:\n- Plant growth under light + nutrient availability\n- Guild-specific uptake differences (root-feeder vs water-column feeder)\n- Algae bloom conditions\n- Competition trade-offs\n- Substrate nutrient cycling\n- Periphyton accumulation\n\nCurrent test files: `cycling.rs`, `chemistry.rs`, `dissolved_oxygen.rs`, `events.rs`, `water_change_mass_balance.rs`, `tank_size_thermal_response.rs`, `ambient_temperature_action.rs`, `validation.rs`, `save_load.rs`, `determinism.rs` — **none specifically test plant/algae growth**.\n\n---\n\n### State Initialization Snapshot\n\nWhen `TankState::new(seed)` is called:\n```\nTankState {\n  geometry: default 45L tank\n  water: default chemistry (clean)\n  substrate_layers: vec![InertSand, 3cm deep, 0 nutrients]\n  plant_guilds: vec![\n    FastStem { biomass: 5g, health: 0.8 },\n    RootRosette { biomass: 3g, health: 0.8 }\n  ]\n  algae: AlgaeState {\n    suspended: 0g,\n    periphyton: 0.2g,\n    nuisance: 0.1\n  }\n  microbe: (seeded cycle state from loop 4)\n  ... rest of state\n}\n```\n\nThe `seeded_example()` variant sets up:\n```\nsubstrate_layers: vec![\n  ActivePlanted { depth: 2cm, N: 40mg, P: 10mg, cEC: 0.8 },\n  CoarsePorous { depth: 1cm, N: 5mg, P: 1mg }\n]\n```\n\nBut **no simulation step ever reads these nutrient amounts**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Component | Exists | Structure | Kinetics | Tests |\n|-----------|--------|-----------|----------|-------|\n| Plant guilds | ✓ | FastStem, RootRosette | ✗ None | ✗ |\n| Plant biomass | ✓ | in state | ✓ Respiration only | ✗ |\n| Plant growth | ✗ | - | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Algae state | ✓ | suspended+periphyton | ✓ Respiration only | ✗ |\n| Algae growth | ✗ | - | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Substrate types | ✓ | 4 kinds | ✗ No dynamics | ✗ |\n| Substrate nutrients | ✓ | N+P stores | ✗ Never consumed | ✗ |\n| Light schedule | ✓ | photoperiod | ✓ Used in O2/DIC | ✗ Growth tests |\n| Plant presets | ✓ | growth_rate, uptake_bias | ✗ Never loaded | ✗ |\n| Substrate presets | ✓ | cEC, trap_index, nutrients | ✗ Never loaded | ✗ |\n| Process params | ✓ | photosynthesis rate | ✗ No growth params | ✗ |\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Implementation Order for Loop 5\n\nBased on spec section 10.7 and 10.8, here's the minimal viable order:\n\n1. **Plant growth system** (use light, nutrients, temperature, guild traits)\n2. **Nutrient uptake from water column** (N, P consumed by plant growth)\n3. **Substrate nutrient integration** (rooted plants access substrate stores differently)\n4. **Algae growth system** (competing with plants for nutrients, affected by shading)\n5. **Competition mechanics** (plant shading reduces algae, excess nutrients drive algae)\n6. **Daily update** for substrate/plant state changes\n7. **Event emission** for bloom/stress conditions\n8. **Acceptance tests** validating guild differences, substrate effects, bloom conditions\n\nThe path does NOT require any other systems: TAN/nitrate/phosphate already tracked, light already computed, temperature already dynamic, pH already responds to plant photosynthesis.\n\n---\n\n### Key Files You'll Need to Modify/Create\n\n**Core additions**:\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate_dynamics.rs` (new, if substrate microbiology warranted)\n\n**Core modifications**:\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — wire plant/algae growth into hourly pipeline\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` — add plant/algae kinetic parameters\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` — expose algae biomass\n\n**Data**:\n- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` — plant/algae growth rate parameters\n\n**Tests**:\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/plant_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/algae_growth.rs` (new)\n\n---\n\nThis completes the thorough analysis. The substrate/plant/algae infrastructure is **structurally complete but functionally inert** — ready for kinetics implementation."},{"type":"text","text":"agentId: ad9d84f2550a80a7e (for resuming to continue this agent's work if needed)\n<usage>total_tokens: 69407\ntool_uses: 41\nduration_ms: 86642</usage>"}]}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8646385e-534a-4d68-9ebc-889753621e92","uuid":"f8fac5e1-2702-4535-9a5e-973a3fa441c7","tool_use_result":{"status":"completed","prompt":"I need to understand what has been implemented in a Rust tank simulation project to plan the next feature (milestone 5: substrate, plants, algae/periphyton).\n\nPlease do the following:\n\n1. Read the specs from previous loops:\n   - loops/001-*/spec.md (or similar)\n   - loops/002-*/spec.md\n   - loops/003-*/spec.md\n   - loops/004-*/spec.md\n\n2. Check what substrate-related code already exists in tank_core:\n   - Any substrate types/structs\n   - Any plant types/structs\n   - Any algae/periphyton types\n   - The current TankState struct definition\n   - The current update pipeline (hourly and daily)\n\n3. Check what TOML presets exist in tank_data for substrate and plants\n\n4. Check which acceptance tests already exist and pass\n\nBe very thorough - I need to know exactly what substrate/plant/algae code exists (even if stubbed) vs what needs to be built from scratch.","agentId":"ad9d84f2550a80a7e","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now I have a comprehensive understanding. Let me create a detailed report.\n\n## Summary: Tank Simulation Project - Current State Analysis\n\nI've thoroughly analyzed the tank simulation project to understand what has been implemented for Milestone 5 (substrate, plants, algae/periphyton). Here's what I found:\n\n### Current Loop Status\nThe project has **successfully completed Loops 1-4**:\n- **Loop 1**: Workspace skeleton, core types, RNG, save/load ✓\n- **Loop 2**: Source water mixing and thermal response ✓\n- **Loop 3**: Dissolved pool dynamics, DO model, pH updates, event emission ✓\n- **Loop 4**: Detritus mineralization, nitrifier guild cycling, biofilter maturation ✓\n\nThe next milestone to implement is **Loop 5 / Milestone 5: Substrate, Plants, Algae/Periphyton**.\n\n---\n\n### What EXISTS (Already Implemented)\n\n#### 1. **Substrate Types & State Structure**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/substrate.rs`\n\n```rust\npub enum SubstrateKind {\n    InertSand,\n    InertGravel,\n    ActivePlanted,\n    CoarsePorous,\n}\n\npub struct SubstrateLayerState {\n    pub kind: SubstrateKind,\n    pub depth_cm: f64,\n    pub nutrient_store_mg_n_total: f64,\n    pub nutrient_store_mg_p_total: f64,\n    pub cation_exchange_capacity_index: f64,\n    pub detritus_trapping_index: f64,\n    pub colonizable_area_cm2: f64,\n    pub low_oxygen_tendency_index: f64,\n    pub grazing_surface_index: f64,\n}\n```\n\n**Key point**: The structure is fully defined with physical properties but **nutrient stores are NOT USED in any update system yet**. They're placeholders.\n\n#### 2. **Plant Guild Types & State**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`\n\n```rust\npub enum PlantGuild {\n    FastStem,\n    RootFeedingRosette,\n}\n\npub struct PlantGuildState {\n    pub guild: PlantGuild,\n    pub biomass_g: f64,\n    pub health_index: f64,\n    pub crowding_index: f64,\n    pub habitat_index: f64,\n}\n```\n\n**Status**: \n- Defined but **no growth/decay system exists**\n- `TankState` always initializes with 2 default plant guilds (8g total at default seed)\n- Biomass changes only via `PlayerAction::TrimPlants { fraction }` action\n- **No nutrient uptake, light dependence, or growth mechanics**\n\n#### 3. **Algae & Periphyton Types**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/biology.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct AlgaeState {\n    pub suspended_biomass_g: f64,          // green water\n    pub periphyton_biomass_g: f64,          // attached biofilm + algae complex\n    pub nuisance_index: f64,                // trouble indicator\n}\n```\n\n**Status**:\n- Defined but **completely inert** in the hourly update pipeline\n- Default: 0g suspended, 0.2g periphyton, 0.1 nuisance_index\n- **No growth, decay, light response, or nutrient interaction**\n\n#### 4. **Periphyton Used in O2/DIC Calculations**\n**Files**: \n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs`\n- `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs`\n\n```rust\npub(crate) fn photosynthetic_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    plant_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g  // <-- both contribute\n}\n\npub(crate) fn respiring_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    let algae_biomass_g = state.algae.suspended_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g;\n    let microbe_biomass_g = /* ... */;\n    let shrimp_biomass_g = /* ... */;\n    // All contribute to O2 demand and DIC respiration\n}\n```\n\n**Status**: Plants and algae **do respire and photosynthesize** (affecting DO and DIC/pH hourly), but they **don't grow or change biomass**.\n\n#### 5. **Plant/Algae Snapshot Exposure**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct TankSnapshot {\n    // ... water chemistry fields ...\n    pub total_plant_biomass_g: f64,  // aggregated plant guild biomass\n    // ... no algae exposure in snapshot yet\n}\n```\n\n#### 6. **Process Parameters for Plants/Algae**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs`\n\n```rust\npub struct ProcessParams {\n    pub plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour: f64,  // rate per g plant biomass\n    pub respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour: f64,\n    pub photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour: f64,\n    // ... no plant-growth kinetics yet\n}\n```\n\nDefault values: `plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour = 0.2`.\n\n#### 7. **TOML Presets Exist**\n**Substrate presets** (`/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/substrate/`):\n- `inert_sand.toml`: cEC=0.1, detritus_trap=0.3, no nutrient charge\n- `inert_gravel.toml`: similar\n- `active_planted.toml`: cEC=0.9, detritus_trap=0.6, N=60mg, P=18mg charge\n- `coarse_porous.toml`: similar structure\n\n**Plant presets** (`/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_data/data/plants/`):\n- `fast_stem.toml`: growth_rate_index=0.9, water_column_uptake=0.9, substrate_uptake=0.2\n- `root_rosette.toml`: growth_rate_index=0.6, water_column_uptake=0.3, substrate_uptake=0.9\n\n**Status**: Presets are **loaded and structured** but **not used during simulation** — they're only metadata.\n\n#### 8. **Player Actions**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`\n\nThe `TrimPlants { fraction }` action is **partially implemented**:\n```rust\nPlayerAction::TrimPlants { fraction } => {\n    for plant in &mut self.state.plant_guilds {\n        plant.biomass_g *= 1.0 - fraction;\n    }\n}\n```\n\nThis simply **scales biomass down** without regrowth mechanics.\n\n#### 9. **Light System**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/light.rs`\n\n```rust\npub fn is_light_on(hour_of_day: u8, photoperiod_hours: f64) -> bool {\n    let start = (12.0 - photoperiod_hours / 2.0) as u8;\n    let end = (12.0 + photoperiod_hours / 2.0) as u8;\n    hour_of_day >= start && hour_of_day < end\n}\n```\n\nLight state is **computed hourly** and passed through the DO and DIC systems, but **plants don't have light-dependent growth**.\n\n---\n\n### What DOES NOT EXIST (Needs Implementation for Milestone 5)\n\n#### 1. **Plant Growth System**\n- **No hourly/daily plant biomass update** based on:\n  - Available light (f_light)\n  - Water temperature (f_temp)\n  - Nutrient availability from water column vs substrate (guild-dependent)\n  - Self-shading and competition\n  - Health/stress modifiers\n- **No respiration-driven senescence**\n- **No habitat-index driving growth potential**\n- **Guild differences are NOT used** (fast-stem should grow faster under water-column nutrients, root-feeder should benefit more from substrate)\n\n#### 2. **Substrate Nutrient Dynamics**\n- Substrate `nutrient_store_mg_n_total` and `nutrient_store_mg_p_total` are **defined but never change**\n- **No plant nutrient uptake from substrate**\n- **No cation-exchange capacity used** (cEC index exists but inactive)\n- **No detritus trapping** (detritus_trapping_index exists but unused)\n- **No microbial activity in substrate microzones**\n\n#### 3. **Algae Growth System**\n- `AlgaeState` (suspended and periphyton) **never changes**\n- **No growth rate formula** based on:\n  - Excess nutrients (N, P) relative to plant uptake\n  - Light availability\n  - Temperature\n  - Grazing pressure (no microfauna system yet)\n  - Competition with plants\n- **No algae bloom mechanic** when plants are weak and nutrients available\n- **No periphyton buildup on surfaces** with increasing colonizable area\n\n#### 4. **Competition Mechanics**\n- **No plant vs algae trade-off** based on light, nutrients, crowding\n- `crowding_index` and `habitat_index` on plants **exist but unused**\n- `nuisance_index` on algae **exists but unused**\n\n#### 5. **Nutrient Uptake Pathways**\n- Water-column nutrients (N, P) are **never removed by plants**\n- Substrate nutrients are **never consumed by plants**\n- **No guild-specific uptake bias** (water-column vs substrate preference)\n- Plants can't compete for scarce nutrients (all growth is zero anyway)\n\n#### 6. **Update Pipeline Integration**\n**File**: `/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs`\n\nThe hourly `step_one_hour` pipeline includes:\n1. Water temperature update\n2. Light state computation\n3. Nitrogen cycle (feed → detritus → mineralization → nitrification)\n4. Chemistry (DIC, alkalinity, pH)\n5. Dissolved oxygen (reaeration, BOD, photosynthetic O2)\n6. Event emission\n\n**Missing**: \n- **No plant growth step** after nutrient/light availability is known\n- **No algae growth step** competing with plants\n- **No daily substrate biogeochemistry** (microbial activity, nutrient cycling)\n- **No plant senescence or stress response to poor conditions**\n\n#### 7. **Linked Systems Not Yet Integrated**\nEven though substrate layer properties are defined, they're not used because:\n- **Periphyton colonizable area** (`colonizable_area_cm2`) is static in SubstrateLayerState\n- **Grazing surface index** doesn't drive microfauna-plant-algae food web (microfauna system is Loop 6)\n- **Low oxygen tendency** in substrate exists but no anoxic microzones are modeled\n- **Detritus trapping** doesn't feed back into local mineralization rates\n\n#### 8. **Acceptance Tests**\nNo tests exist for:\n- Plant growth under light + nutrient availability\n- Guild-specific uptake differences (root-feeder vs water-column feeder)\n- Algae bloom conditions\n- Competition trade-offs\n- Substrate nutrient cycling\n- Periphyton accumulation\n\nCurrent test files: `cycling.rs`, `chemistry.rs`, `dissolved_oxygen.rs`, `events.rs`, `water_change_mass_balance.rs`, `tank_size_thermal_response.rs`, `ambient_temperature_action.rs`, `validation.rs`, `save_load.rs`, `determinism.rs` — **none specifically test plant/algae growth**.\n\n---\n\n### State Initialization Snapshot\n\nWhen `TankState::new(seed)` is called:\n```\nTankState {\n  geometry: default 45L tank\n  water: default chemistry (clean)\n  substrate_layers: vec![InertSand, 3cm deep, 0 nutrients]\n  plant_guilds: vec![\n    FastStem { biomass: 5g, health: 0.8 },\n    RootRosette { biomass: 3g, health: 0.8 }\n  ]\n  algae: AlgaeState {\n    suspended: 0g,\n    periphyton: 0.2g,\n    nuisance: 0.1\n  }\n  microbe: (seeded cycle state from loop 4)\n  ... rest of state\n}\n```\n\nThe `seeded_example()` variant sets up:\n```\nsubstrate_layers: vec![\n  ActivePlanted { depth: 2cm, N: 40mg, P: 10mg, cEC: 0.8 },\n  CoarsePorous { depth: 1cm, N: 5mg, P: 1mg }\n]\n```\n\nBut **no simulation step ever reads these nutrient amounts**.\n\n---\n\n### Summary Table\n\n| Component | Exists | Structure | Kinetics | Tests |\n|-----------|--------|-----------|----------|-------|\n| Plant guilds | ✓ | FastStem, RootRosette | ✗ None | ✗ |\n| Plant biomass | ✓ | in state | ✓ Respiration only | ✗ |\n| Plant growth | ✗ | - | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Algae state | ✓ | suspended+periphyton | ✓ Respiration only | ✗ |\n| Algae growth | ✗ | - | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Substrate types | ✓ | 4 kinds | ✗ No dynamics | ✗ |\n| Substrate nutrients | ✓ | N+P stores | ✗ Never consumed | ✗ |\n| Light schedule | ✓ | photoperiod | ✓ Used in O2/DIC | ✗ Growth tests |\n| Plant presets | ✓ | growth_rate, uptake_bias | ✗ Never loaded | ✗ |\n| Substrate presets | ✓ | cEC, trap_index, nutrients | ✗ Never loaded | ✗ |\n| Process params | ✓ | photosynthesis rate | ✗ No growth params | ✗ |\n\n---\n\n### Recommended Implementation Order for Loop 5\n\nBased on spec section 10.7 and 10.8, here's the minimal viable order:\n\n1. **Plant growth system** (use light, nutrients, temperature, guild traits)\n2. **Nutrient uptake from water column** (N, P consumed by plant growth)\n3. **Substrate nutrient integration** (rooted plants access substrate stores differently)\n4. **Algae growth system** (competing with plants for nutrients, affected by shading)\n5. **Competition mechanics** (plant shading reduces algae, excess nutrients drive algae)\n6. **Daily update** for substrate/plant state changes\n7. **Event emission** for bloom/stress conditions\n8. **Acceptance tests** validating guild differences, substrate effects, bloom conditions\n\nThe path does NOT require any other systems: TAN/nitrate/phosphate already tracked, light already computed, temperature already dynamic, pH already responds to plant photosynthesis.\n\n---\n\n### Key Files You'll Need to Modify/Create\n\n**Core additions**:\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/algae_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/src/systems/substrate_dynamics.rs` (new, if substrate microbiology warranted)\n\n**Core modifications**:\n- `crates/tank_core/src/engine.rs` — wire plant/algae growth into hourly pipeline\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/process.rs` — add plant/algae kinetic parameters\n- `crates/tank_core/src/types/snapshot.rs` — expose algae biomass\n\n**Data**:\n- `crates/tank_data/data/process/default.toml` — plant/algae growth rate parameters\n\n**Tests**:\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/plant_growth.rs` (new)\n- `crates/tank_core/tests/algae_growth.rs` (new)\n\n---\n\nThis completes the thorough analysis. The substrate/plant/algae infrastructure is **structurally complete but functionally inert** — ready for kinetics implementation."}],"totalDurationMs":86642,"totalTokens":69407,"totalToolUseCount":41,"usage":{"input_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1941,"cache_read_input_tokens":63194,"output_tokens":4272,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1941},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[],"speed":"standard"}}}
